TRADEMARK AND BRAND ASSETS — NOT COVERED BY THE MIT LICENCE ABOVE

The MIT licence above applies to the source code only. It does NOT grant any
right to use the following, which remain the property of ownCoder:

  - the name "Tabcove", and any confusingly similar name
  - the Tabcove logo and the icon set in extension/icons/, assets/, and site/
  - the promotional artwork in Store Upload/Store Assets/

If you fork, modify, or redistribute this software, you must do so under a
DIFFERENT name and a DIFFERENT mark, and you must not represent your version as
being published or endorsed by ownCoder.

This restriction exists to protect users, not to restrict developers. In this
exact software category, a widely-installed tab-management extension was
acquired by new owners in 2020 and re-published under its original name with
code that executed arbitrary remote instructions; it was removed from the Chrome
Web Store in February 2021, by which time it had been installed by more than two
million people who had no way to tell the trusted version from the malicious
one. Keeping the name and the mark tied to a single publisher is what makes that
distinction possible.
